BT /F2 16 Tf 72 710 Td (Chapter 4 – Still and Full) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 680 Td (Rue sat under the mushroom until the moon was high.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 662 Td (She did not chase anything.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 644 Td (She did not climb anything.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 626 Td (She just listened, and the forest filled her right up.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 608 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 590 Td (When she finally curled her tail around herself to sleep,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 572 Td (she felt fuller than she had after the longest, busiest day.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 554 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 536 Td ("Tomorrow," she thought with a smile, "I will be still for a little while first.") Tj ET
